  message: "P3 REVIEW 2026-11-01 (dev 100b6fbb6e; owner-requested re-check of open P3 items last modified before 2026-10-20; fixtures under ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/p3_review_11012026/taint1/). VERDICT: PARTLY-STALE. 2026-11-01 review on dev 100b6fbb6e: parts 1 and 3 reproduce (Java/C '(flag && (v = g(n)) != null)' def=[v] use=[flag,n]; Java/C 'a.f = v' reads a; TS 'this.a = v' / Python 'self.a = v' define the receiver without reading it). Part 2 is no longer a divergence: e926fc1045 (PR #1790) removed WI-tozar's CONTAINED-ONLY rule, so TS 'acc.push(k = g(n))' now also gives def=[k] use=[acc,n] like Java/C, and the JS walk hole was closed by WI-tinav. Drop part 2. MECHANISM: Java/C def/use do not apply weak-update semantics to conditionally executed nested bindings; TS/Python statement-level receiver writes are strong. SHARES MECHANISM WITH: WI-jahip."  # 1347
